## Expected failure, documented not fixed: Patch rasterizes no pixels.
## SPEC.md Section 8 ("Found by running the corpus after phase 3 landed"):
## confirmed on a minimal single-Patch RIB with no archive, gzip, or
## near-clip precision concern -- a rendering-pipeline gap distinct from
## the (fixed) RIB front-end defects that used to keep bikeData.rib.gz's
## own ~5,300 Patch requests from ever reaching the parser at all. Out of
## this phase's scope (Patch tessellation, not the RIB front end) --
## reported, not fixed. No golden minted for this scene: a Patch that
## never rasterizes has nothing meaningful to regress against.
##
## A Sphere shares the scene as a control: same lighting, same shader,
## proving the renderer itself works and the gap is Patch-specific.
Display "patch_norender.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Sides 2
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
AttributeBegin
	Translate -1 0 0
	Patch "bilinear" "P" [-0.5 -0.5 0  0.5 -0.5 0  -0.5 0.5 0  0.5 0.5 0]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 1 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
